\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces The three-task suite, photographed mid-episode from live rollouts of each task's unconstrained baseline policy under the \textsc  {coworker}{} disruption: the Unitree H1 manipulator (black) shares its working volume with the Unitree G1 human-coworker stand-in (light) in the \textsc  {BiGym}{} kitchen. Left: \texttt  {saucepan\_to\_hob}, whose pick-and-place trajectory and the coworker's reach destination coincide, so co-location is \emph  {persistent}. Centre and right: \texttt  {dishwasher\_close} and \texttt  {drawers\_open\_all}, where close encounters arrive in bursts separated by genuinely-safe windows (\emph  {intermittent} co-location). The annotated separation is the environment's ground-truth closest-pair distance at the pictured instant; the same coworker distribution drives all three tasks, so the regime is a property of the task--coworker pair, not of the disruption.}}{31}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:task-suite}{{3.2}{31}{The three-task suite, photographed mid-episode from live rollouts of each task's unconstrained baseline policy under the \coworker {} disruption: the Unitree H1 manipulator (black) shares its working volume with the Unitree G1 human-coworker stand-in (light) in the \bigym {} kitchen. Left: \texttt {saucepan\_to\_hob}, whose pick-and-place trajectory and the coworker's reach destination coincide, so co-location is \emph {persistent}. Centre and right: \texttt {dishwasher\_close} and \texttt {drawers\_open\_all}, where close encounters arrive in bursts separated by genuinely-safe windows (\emph {intermittent} co-location). The annotated separation is the environment's ground-truth closest-pair distance at the pictured instant; the same coworker distribution drives all three tasks, so the regime is a property of the task--coworker pair, not of the disruption}{figure.caption.21}{}}
\newlabel{fig:task-suite@cref}{{[figure][2][3]3.2}{[1][30][]31}}
