\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces The two-axis division of labour on \texttt  {saucepan\_to\_hob} (60-episode cells, \texttt  {noisy} perception, \textsc  {coworker}{} distribution) and what composing the specialists buys. The policy owns the proximity axis, the graded speed-scaling filter owns the velocity axis, and only their composition reaches the corner where both ISO~15066{} axes improve at once, at a success cost ($0.85 \to 0.44$) that Section~\ref {sec:results:boundary} shows to be the persistent regime's ceiling rather than a tuning defect.}}{53}{figure.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
