\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.4}{\ignorespaces Experiment E5.1. Separation statistics across the headline configurations (\textsc  {coworker}{}, \texttt  {noisy}). The policy improves the \emph  {mean} separation but the worst-case tail ($\ensuremath  {\mathrm  {CVaR}}_{0.95}$ and the single worst approach) is unchanged, because the closest approach is the coworker's lunge toward a robot it is co-located with, an \emph  {exogenous} event no robot-action policy or filter can remove. The controllable quantity is the dwell and frequency of proximity, not the single worst-case approach.}}{55}{table.caption.55}\protected@file@percent }
